  <p>
    ✅ <term>Do this:</term> What are the null and alternative
    hypotheses for the test this statistic is used for?
  </p>

  <p>
    ###ANSWER## The null hypothesis is that there is no relationship
    between the output variable and the input variables. The alternative
    hypothesis is that at least one input variable is related to the
    output variable.
  </p>

  <p>
    ✅ <term>Do this:</term> What is your conclusion of the test given
    this F-score?
  </p>

  <program language="python">
  <code>
##ANSWER##
# If we just want the p-value
est.f_pvalue
# Note very small, so we will reject the null hypothesis and conclude that SOME 
# input variable is related to the output variable. Note that this does not tell
# us which one it is
  </code>
  </program>

