<section xml:id="q2-subsets-of-variables">
  <title>Q2: Subsets of variables</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      ✅ <term>Q:</term> List all 6 subsets of the three variables being
      used.
    </p>

    <p>
      ##ANSWER## - TV - Radio - Newspaper - TV, Radio - TV, Newspaper -
      Radio, Newspaper - TV, Radio, Newspaper
    </p>

    <p>
      ✅ <term>Do this:</term> Below is a command to get the RSS for the
      statsmodel linear fit. For each of the subsets listed above, what
      is the RSS for the learned model? Which is smallest?
    </p>

    <program language="python">
    <code>
def statsmodelRSS(est):
    # Returns the RSS for the statsmodel ols class
    return np.sum(est.resid**2)
    </code>
    </program>

    <program language="python">
    <code>
est.ssr
# print(statsmodelRSS(est))
    </code>
    </program>

    <pre>
556.8252629021874
    </pre>

    <program language="python">
    <code>
##ANSWER##
import itertools 

variables = ['TV', 'Radio', 'Newspaper']
for i in range(1,4): # Want 1, 2, 3
    for subset in itertools.combinations(variables,i):
        model = 'Sales ~ ' + " + ".join(subset)
        print(model)
        est = smf.ols(model, advertising_df).fit()
        print(np.round(statsmodelRSS(est),2))
    
# Best job done by all three or TV and Radio
    </code>
    </program>

